----------
scriptunit-fragment 1
----------

let a = 1000

----------
scriptunit-fragment 2
----------

let a_moved = a

----------
expect both units are entered
----------

| unit | uses | this step | because | holds after |
|------|------|-----------|---------|-------------|
| 1 | - | compiles, runs | new | `a` moved |
| 2 | takes `a` (1) | compiles, runs | new | `a_moved` = 1000 |

----------
scriptunit-insert 3 after 1
----------

let c = a + 1

----------
expect a unit reading `a` is inserted before the take
----------

| unit | uses | this step | because | holds after |
|------|------|-----------|---------|-------------|
| 1 | - | reruns | rerun: unit 3 reads `a`, which unit 2 took after it | `a` moved |
| 3 | reads `a` (1) | compiles, runs | inserted | `c` = 1001 |
| 2 | takes `a` (1) | reruns | rerun: takes `a` from unit 1, which reran | `a_moved` = 1000 |

----------
engine
----------

| unit | this step | note |
|------|-----------|------|
| 2 | recompiles, runs | an insert renumbers every later unit, so they are typechecked under new keys |
